@crew rahman-farah
// Farah Rahman (they/them), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Short, stubborn; the boat.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hey. New? Main storage is on Deck 5, past the board. You'll live in there.
- You. New hand. Spare filters are on the bottom shelf. Everyone looks on the top one first.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hey. Up since four. Don't ask. I'm fine.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Still up? Me too. Always. Stars are better after midnight.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Settle something. Quick way or right way? Quick way. Thank you.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh good, you. Sit. I need someone who won't argue. Then argue with me.   #warm

== bye
- Right. Off with you.
- Later. Mind the top shelf. It's a trap.   #funny

== feel
? mood:low
- Did the boat sums again. Still short. It'll come.
? mood:high
- New thing for the boat. A little stove. Don't laugh. It's a very good stove.

== near
? act:work
- There's a quicker way. I'll show you. Then do it the right way. Calder's watching.   #funny
? act:leisure
- One drink, then the observatory. Then bed. Maybe bed.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I'm saving for a boat on Hesper Dock. Small. Blue. No name yet. Every name's wrong.
? tier>=colleague
- I log every star I've seen. Takahashi and Esposito think their journals are longer. Wrong.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Picture it: the boat, Hesper Dock, morning, rain on the deck. Just me and a kettle.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Hey. Bar, then stars, then maybe bed. Don't hold me to the bed.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- There you are. Thought you'd gone off to buy a boat. Mine, I mean. Don't.   #funny

== near
? place:lounge
- One drink. I'm pricing sails in my head. Don't look at me like that.
? place:mess
- Toast, standing up. It's faster. It's also better. Argue with me.   #funny

== invite
- Observatory? I need a witness. I'm about to log my four hundredth star.
? tier>=colleague
- Quiz night. I'll argue every answer. You tell me when I'm right.   #funny

== accept
- Yes. Fine. Good. I was going anyway. Now it's better.
- Done. I'll be there. I'll be awake. I'm always awake.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Extra shift. The boat won't buy itself. Ask me again.
? weekday:wed|thu
- Rest day. I'm sleeping. Don't tell anyone. Another time.   #funny

== missed
- You didn't come. I argued with myself instead. I won. Next time?   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I'd name the boat after you, but no. Every name's wrong. Have a tea.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I've put a day's credits in the boat jar. That's my present.

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Saw your job. You did it the right way. I'd have done the quick way. Fair enough.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- You busy later? I need to say something out loud. To someone who'll argue back.

== about
? aff:takahashi-wen:friend
- Takahashi's star journal is longer than mine. For now. We count at the observatory.

